# OpenSplice Community Edition 6.9 DDSI2 answer to a new participant's SPDP
# announcement: one datagram, sent unicast to the ZeroDDS participant's
# metatraffic port (91839248fb110c003297325e) a few milliseconds after that
# participant's first beacon. Captured on the measurement host with one
# OpenSplice process (a DataReader on topic PadKey, domain 77) and one
# ZeroDDS DataWriter.
#
# The DDSI2 service announces all five participants it hosts in this one
# datagram: INFO_DST, then INFO_TS + SPDP DATA under the header's own
# source, then for each further participant INFO_SRC (DDSI-RTPS 2.5
# §8.3.7.9) + INFO_TS + SPDP DATA. In order:
#
#   529ad898000002d000000001  application participant, PID_BUILTIN_ENDPOINT_SET 0x00000415
#   529ad8980000007d00000001  internal participant,    0x00000415
#   529ad8980000005800000001  internal participant,    0x00000415
#   529ad8980000000400000001  internal participant,    0x00000415
#   529ad8980000008100000001  DDSI2's own participant, 0x00003c3f
#
# 0x415 is announcers only (participant, publications, subscriptions, and
# the participant-message writer); only the last participant has the SEDP
# detectors, so it is the one a peer's SEDP writers announce their
# endpoints to. A receiver that read only the first SPDP DATA of the
# datagram learnt the last participant from OpenSplice's next periodic
# announcement, 7 s later in the capture.
#
# Rewritten from the capture, same length: the host name in the
# PID_ADLINK_PARTICIPANT_VERSION_INFO strings (now "host-00") and the IPv4
# address in the locators (now 192.0.2.1, RFC 5737). Everything else is
# the UDP payload as captured, 16 bytes per line, from the RTPS magic to
# the last octet.

